1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:01,940
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,610
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,610 --> 00:00:05,110
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,450
Ma'am. I'm sorry, but this item...

5
00:00:07,510 --> 00:00:10,520
was only offered to 100 VIPs
5 years ago,

6
00:00:10,580 --> 00:00:11,950
so it's no longer available
for purchase.

7
00:00:26,560 --> 00:00:28,570
Can I get this exact same model?

8
00:00:30,170 --> 00:00:31,200
This was...

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,510
only offered to 100 VIPs
5 years ago,

10
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:35,970
so it isn't available
for purchase, ma'am.

11
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:39,280
Then is there anything similar?

12
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,180
The gloves belong to Director Joo?

13
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:48,690
But one of them...

14
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:51,960
was found at the scene
of Attorney Seo's accident.

15
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:56,090
Why was Director Joo there?

16
00:01:16,010 --> 00:01:17,050
Are you asleep, my daughter?

17
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:20,190
Daddy misses you like crazy.

18
00:01:21,090 --> 00:01:22,290
I'll see you tomorrow, right?

19
00:01:34,200 --> 00:01:35,200
Hae Ra.

20
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,140
Did something happen?

21
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:43,740
You've seemed upset
for the past few days.

22
00:01:44,980 --> 00:01:45,980
No.

23
00:01:46,040 --> 00:01:47,210
I'm going to sleep, so please leave.

24
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,950
Don't be like this, Hae Ra.
Talk to me.

25
00:01:51,250 --> 00:01:52,280
Talk about what?

26
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,220
Can you just leave me alone?

27
00:01:56,150 --> 00:01:57,460
What's bothering you?

28
00:01:58,660 --> 00:02:01,030
Tell me.
I'll take care of everything.

29
00:02:02,930 --> 00:02:05,300
Take care of what?
How could you possibly fix this?

30
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:08,800
Are you my mom or something?

31
00:02:12,270 --> 00:02:15,040
Unless you're my mom,
mind your own business.

32
00:02:28,950 --> 00:02:32,420
You've got to be kidding me!

33
00:02:32,890 --> 00:02:34,530
Why? Did something happen again?

34
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:36,860
The rumor...

35
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:41,000
It's already spread everywhere.

36
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:42,900
Wait, what rumor?

37
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:44,270
That my eldest grandson...

38
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:47,110
is fooling around
with a single mother.

39
00:02:47,510 --> 00:02:50,910
From the tofu shop to the butcher's,
everyone knows about it.

40
00:02:51,280 --> 00:02:53,650
No way. How did they find out?

41
00:02:54,580 --> 00:02:57,250
They said the two were practically
filming a movie in the shop.

42
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:00,290
Hugging each other,
completely head over heels.

43
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:04,790
Well, I'm fond of Teun Teun's mom.

44
00:03:05,390 --> 00:03:08,560
Honestly, as a daughter-in-law,
she'd be a true blessing.

45
00:03:08,660 --> 00:03:09,660
What?

46
00:03:09,990 --> 00:03:13,100
Well, it's true.
She manages the household so well,

47
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,970
and she knows
how to respect her elders.

48
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:17,240
Respect, my foot.

49
00:03:18,470 --> 00:03:21,170
That woman is as cold as ice.

50
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,410
Plus, if they end up
getting married,

51
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:26,840
we get a cute grandson as a bonus.

52
00:03:27,080 --> 00:03:28,310
Isn't that great?

53
00:03:28,550 --> 00:03:30,250
You mindless fool.

54
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:32,320
A grandson who isn't even our blood?

55
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:33,850
Right. Sounds wonderful.

56
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:37,960
I support Eun Guk
marrying Teun Teun's mom.

57
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:39,020
I'm all for it.

58
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,490
He can marry her after I'm dead.

59
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:45,660
Because while I'm still breathing,
it'll never happen.

60
00:03:45,860 --> 00:03:48,730
Looks like they'll only have to wait
until next spring.

61
00:03:49,230 --> 00:03:51,170
What? What was that?

62
00:03:51,570 --> 00:03:55,370
Are you saying your mom
is going to drop dead next spring?

63
00:03:55,710 --> 00:03:58,840
You always struggle
with the yellow dust every spring,

64
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,850
always complaining about
how it messes with your breathing.

65
00:04:00,950 --> 00:04:01,980
What?

66
00:04:02,850 --> 00:04:04,180
- You dare dodge?
- Unbelievable.

67
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,920
Come on.

68
00:04:06,950 --> 00:04:08,850
Let's limit hitting to once a day.

69
00:04:08,850 --> 00:04:10,560
Darn, my arm.

70
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:19,200
Are you my mom or something?

71
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:23,500
Unless you're my mom,
mind your own business.

72
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:35,510
It's me.

73
00:04:35,780 --> 00:04:37,350
Any word on An Guk Cheol yet?

74
00:04:38,080 --> 00:04:39,850
We got the CCTV footage
from the engagement venue...

75
00:04:40,050 --> 00:04:41,490
and are currently tracking
his movements.

76
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:43,920
You're still not done with that?

77
00:04:44,390 --> 00:04:46,020
Since this isn't
an official investigation,

78
00:04:46,220 --> 00:04:47,990
it took a while
to grease a few palms.

79
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:49,460
I apologize.

80
00:04:49,890 --> 00:04:51,160
Find him as soon as possible.

81
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,400
Money isn't an issue.

82
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:12,880
You jerk.

83
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:16,690
Just wait until I catch you.

84
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:29,730
As if you're even worthy
of designer brands.

85
00:05:33,540 --> 00:05:35,140
Yes. Come in.

86
00:05:36,940 --> 00:05:38,410
You're here. Have a seat.

87
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:45,950
Here.

88
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,250
These are the gloves you mentioned.

89
00:05:48,950 --> 00:05:51,060
I used to wear them to every event.

90
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:54,030
You'll be going to plenty of those
soon enough,

91
00:05:54,090 --> 00:05:55,330
so you'll need them, right?

92
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,660
Yes, thank you.

93
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:23,190
These don't even come close
to the limited VIP edition.

94
00:06:32,030 --> 00:06:33,970
The candidate list
has been finalized,

95
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:36,730
and interviews will begin
as scheduled early next month.

96
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:38,870
I heard Eun Seol was a big help.

97
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,000
Good work, both of you.

98
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:41,770
Thank you.

99
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,550
Excuse me, I'm sorry,

100
00:06:55,320 --> 00:06:56,950
but may I use the restroom?

101
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,490
Yes, go ahead.

102
00:07:28,820 --> 00:07:30,960
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

103
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:01,820
Because I can't just take
your word for it anymore.

104
00:08:05,460 --> 00:08:07,730
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

105
00:08:08,960 --> 00:08:10,600
Want to get dinner together then?

106
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:13,100
I checked,
and your favorite restaurant...

107
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:14,130
still has a table open.

108
00:08:14,970 --> 00:08:17,870
No, I want to head home early.
I'm tired.

109
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,040
It's too late to turn back anyway.

110
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:30,180
Now that it has come to this,

111
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:34,220
I'll use Kang Hae Ra to move up.

112
00:08:36,090 --> 00:08:37,220
If I keep climbing, who knows?

113
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,830
Cheongma might just end up...

114
00:08:42,530 --> 00:08:44,000
being mine.

115
00:08:50,070 --> 00:08:51,070
Yes?

116
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:52,740
The CEO is asking for you.

117
00:08:54,410 --> 00:08:55,440
All right.

118
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:05,320
Since you're engaged now,

119
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:08,050
it's time to slowly get ready
for next year's wedding.

120
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:10,150
Yes, sir.

121
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:11,990
Hae Ra and I will start planning
little by little.

122
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:15,460
What do you say we look
for a wedding planner?

123
00:09:15,630 --> 00:09:18,360
Both you and Hae Ra
are so busy right now, Chief Cha.

124
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:19,830
That sounds good as well.

125
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,330
And another thing.

126
00:09:21,330 --> 00:09:24,540
Once you're married,
where will you two settle down?

127
00:09:27,870 --> 00:09:28,940
Well,

128
00:09:29,140 --> 00:09:32,580
your current place wouldn't work,
would it, Chief Cha?

129
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,610
It's a bit far from work,

130
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:37,420
and the place is on the small side.

131
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:40,620
I'll discuss that
with Hae Ra as well.

132
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:43,490
Her opinion is important, of course,

133
00:09:43,920 --> 00:09:46,560
but ours matters more.

134
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:51,030
You seem to keep forgetting this,

135
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:54,430
but this is no ordinary marriage.

136
00:09:55,100 --> 00:09:58,470
It decides whether you become
part of Cheongma or not.

137
00:09:59,070 --> 00:10:00,070
So,

138
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,610
you can't treat this
like any ordinary wedding.

139
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:05,940
Honey,

140
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:08,550
why put so much pressure
on Chief Cha?

141
00:10:09,780 --> 00:10:13,350
Come on.
Don't you feel the same way?

142
00:10:15,850 --> 00:10:16,920
Well, we were thinking...

143
00:10:17,920 --> 00:10:20,260
it'd be best
if you moved in with us.

144
00:10:22,630 --> 00:10:23,960
Then what about my mother?

145
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,960
These days,

146
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:27,800
luxury retirement homes have
great facilities.

147
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:31,770
We could also assign
a dedicated caregiver for So Yeon.

148
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:37,640
I know it's hard to decide
right away.

149
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:41,280
We'll explore
some other options too,

150
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:45,520
so let's figure this out together,
Chief Cha. Okay?

151
00:10:47,050 --> 00:10:48,050
Yes, ma'am.

152
00:10:49,450 --> 00:10:53,020
After all,
we're So Yeon's guardians now too.

153
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:55,330
Chief Cha, when I was a newlywed,

154
00:10:55,730 --> 00:10:56,990
I had to learn everything
from scratch...

155
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:58,830
under my father-in-law.

156
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:03,000
Naturally, you should go through
that same process.

157
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,900
I'll think it over.

158
00:11:09,110 --> 00:11:10,110
Yes,

159
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:13,080
let's take some time
and think about it carefully.

160
00:11:13,710 --> 00:11:14,710
Sure.

161
00:11:17,980 --> 00:11:18,980
Come in.

162
00:11:23,520 --> 00:11:25,690
The CEO asked me
to deliver this to you.

163
00:11:39,100 --> 00:11:40,100
(Premium Noble Care:
A premier life, a true sanctuary)

164
00:11:40,170 --> 00:11:41,170
(Cheongun Gaon
Senior Care Residence)

165
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,770
(Evergreen Forest: Caring with love
for a better tomorrow)

166
00:11:57,820 --> 00:11:59,060
Are you very busy?

167
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:16,740
Right. It's about time
you needed another dose of me.

168
00:12:45,670 --> 00:12:48,270
Here's the promo video budget
for the scholarship program.

169
00:12:51,040 --> 00:12:52,740
Do I only get to see you...

170
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:54,980
when you have something to report?

171
00:12:58,150 --> 00:12:59,180
I'm sorry.

172
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:01,320
I'll drop by more often.

173
00:13:02,390 --> 00:13:04,560
You kept this weekend open, right?

174
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,120
Yes.

175
00:13:06,620 --> 00:13:09,530
I booked a quiet spot
by the sea this time.

176
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,000
The sea?

177
00:13:14,730 --> 00:13:15,870
I like the sound of that.

178
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:18,940
The weekend feels too far away.

179
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:23,010
Am I the only one
who feels that way?

180
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,210
I feel the same.

181
00:13:27,750 --> 00:13:31,350
I want to be by your side
every day too, sir.

182
00:13:31,950 --> 00:13:33,050
Just like the Chairman.

183
00:13:36,620 --> 00:13:37,660
I'm...

184
00:13:38,720 --> 00:13:40,790
so jealous of her.

185
00:13:43,330 --> 00:13:44,400
I know.

186
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,970
It's killing me too.

187
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:54,510
You look so worn out lately.

188
00:13:59,010 --> 00:14:01,750
And whose fault is that?

189
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:09,950
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

190
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:36,750
Hello?

191
00:14:36,850 --> 00:14:37,850
Daughter,

192
00:14:38,450 --> 00:14:39,750
don't you miss your dad?

193
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:44,020
I'll call you back later.

194
00:14:49,730 --> 00:14:52,360
If you call me one more time,
I'll report you to the police.

195
00:14:52,760 --> 00:14:55,500
Don't contact me
until I reach out to you.

196
00:14:58,170 --> 00:15:00,000
If the cops catch me,

197
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,370
it'll be a lot harder on you,
sweetheart.

198
00:15:02,640 --> 00:15:03,640
The police...

199
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:06,340
They always look into
a drifter's family first.

200
00:15:22,760 --> 00:15:24,460
So, what do you want from me?

201
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:28,930
Hae Ra,
your dad has nowhere to sleep.

202
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:33,000
Could my sweet Hae Ra just find
a little place for her dad to stay?

203
00:15:33,940 --> 00:15:37,210
If not, your dad will have to sleep
at the subway station.

204
00:15:37,510 --> 00:15:40,480
But what if the police catch me?

205
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:43,310
Where are you right now? Tell me!

206
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:54,460
Well, for a temporary spot,
it's pretty nice.

207
00:15:55,490 --> 00:15:56,530
What do you mean, temporary?

208
00:15:57,230 --> 00:15:58,760
This place is just a rental.

209
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:00,530
I still have my pride
as your father.

210
00:16:00,960 --> 00:16:02,500
How could I possibly live
in a rental?

211
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:06,170
You're going to be the next head
of Cheongma, after all.

212
00:16:06,700 --> 00:16:08,840
I should at least own a place...

213
00:16:08,910 --> 00:16:10,670
with a view of the Han River.

214
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:13,140
If you don't want to end up
at the bottom of the Han River instead,

215
00:16:13,140 --> 00:16:14,280
you'd better watch yourself.

216
00:16:17,250 --> 00:16:20,120
I call you.
Never the other way around.

217
00:16:20,680 --> 00:16:21,720
And...

218
00:16:22,290 --> 00:16:24,590
don't take one step out of here
without my permission.

219
00:16:24,660 --> 00:16:26,420
Just keep your head down
and stay put.

220
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:27,960
Got it?

221
00:16:28,090 --> 00:16:30,290
Of course.
Whatever my daughter says goes.

222
00:16:30,730 --> 00:16:32,930
I'll be a good dad and listen.

223
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,970
You're my daughter, after all.

224
00:16:34,970 --> 00:16:37,840
Stop calling me your daughter,
darn it!

225
00:16:38,570 --> 00:16:41,540
All right, your dad will do
as you say, my daughter.

226
00:16:43,370 --> 00:16:44,980
My lips are sealed.

227
00:16:45,140 --> 00:16:46,140
Unbelievable!

228
00:16:46,180 --> 00:16:47,980
Get home safely, my daughter.

229
00:16:56,820 --> 00:16:58,390
You can wrap up
the factory inspection...

230
00:16:58,390 --> 00:16:59,390
before the next meeting, right?

231
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:01,830
Yes, I'll make sure
to meet the deadline.

232
00:17:05,700 --> 00:17:06,800
(Cheongun Gaon
Senior Care Residence)

233
00:17:09,370 --> 00:17:10,400
Oh, this?

234
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:13,200
Please tell me I'm wrong.

235
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:14,570
About what?

236
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,110
You're not putting your mother
in a facility, are you?

237
00:17:17,980 --> 00:17:18,980
I'm not.

238
00:17:20,810 --> 00:17:22,150
I know it's not my place,

239
00:17:23,450 --> 00:17:26,150
but I hope
you'll think it over carefully.

240
00:17:27,220 --> 00:17:28,690
It'll break your mother's heart.

241
00:17:29,850 --> 00:17:31,920
Right. Thank you for caring.

242
00:17:33,290 --> 00:17:34,290
Then...

243
00:17:52,310 --> 00:17:54,140
Where did you say he was last seen?

244
00:17:54,710 --> 00:17:56,610
At a foreign car dealership.

245
00:17:56,810 --> 00:17:58,520
A foreign car dealership?

246
00:17:58,950 --> 00:18:00,780
- Why on earth was he there?
- Beats me.

247
00:18:01,720 --> 00:18:04,620
That's why tracking his movements
has been even harder.

248
00:18:04,990 --> 00:18:06,620
It wasn't somewhere
we could easily guess,

249
00:18:06,620 --> 00:18:08,690
but somewhere completely unexpected.

250
00:18:08,890 --> 00:18:11,160
Darn it. He's really lost his mind.

251
00:18:11,230 --> 00:18:12,900
What on earth is he planning?

252
00:18:13,360 --> 00:18:14,670
You hired more people, right?

253
00:18:15,270 --> 00:18:16,900
Yes, we're even covering...

254
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,570
the areas surrounding Seoul
in Gyeonggi Province.

255
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,900
Search everywhere,
no matter how far out.

256
00:18:21,410 --> 00:18:24,070
Put him in a psychiatric hospital
the moment you find him.

257
00:18:24,710 --> 00:18:26,140
Yes, I'll do that.

258
00:18:28,180 --> 00:18:29,180
Jun Hwan.

259
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:34,380
Get your act together, okay?

260
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:38,820
If my life is ruined,
you're going down with me.

261
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:44,460
Because of what happened
to Team Leader Seo,

262
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,300
we're already in the same boat.

263
00:18:47,300 --> 00:18:48,300
Right?

264
00:18:48,730 --> 00:18:49,730
Oh, right.

265
00:18:50,230 --> 00:18:51,240
Of course.

266
00:18:52,200 --> 00:18:53,200
I'll keep that in mind.

267
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:02,750
Director Joo.

268
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:06,450
You're nothing but trash
that stoops to this level.

269
00:19:10,050 --> 00:19:11,050
You'll end up...

270
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:14,630
as another one of her accomplices.

271
00:19:18,530 --> 00:19:19,530
Then,

272
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:22,300
you'll eventually...

273
00:19:23,970 --> 00:19:25,270
meet your end...

274
00:19:26,670 --> 00:19:28,840
at her hands just like Manager Na.

275
00:19:43,190 --> 00:19:44,190
It's me.

276
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:46,790
Let's start by checking
the adult arcades in that area.

277
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:58,540
Is something bothering you?

278
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,210
I'm worried about Teun Teun.

279
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:04,410
Teun Teun?

280
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,450
I haven't told him
about Hyun Jae yet.

281
00:20:11,780 --> 00:20:14,150
I only said he went to the US
on a business trip,

282
00:20:14,220 --> 00:20:18,490
but every evening,
he begs me to video call his uncle.

283
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,030
I'm just wondering
what excuse I should make today.

284
00:20:23,760 --> 00:20:26,230
He really misses Attorney Seo,
doesn't he?

285
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:28,930
Yes.

286
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,530
Ever since he was born,

287
00:20:30,870 --> 00:20:33,100
he's looked up to Hyun Jae
like his own dad.

288
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:38,340
Whenever I tell Teun Teun...

289
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:41,040
where Hyun Jae is staying
in the US right now,

290
00:20:41,650 --> 00:20:43,880
I find myself wanting
to believe it too.

291
00:20:45,380 --> 00:20:46,550
Sometimes it really feels like...

292
00:20:46,850 --> 00:20:49,490
Hyun Jae just went on
a business trip to the US.

293
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:56,390
I'll have to tell Teun Teun
the truth someday, right?

294
00:20:57,560 --> 00:20:58,600
Maybe rather than him,

295
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,730
you're the one who needs more time.

296
00:21:04,500 --> 00:21:07,170
So, don't rush yourself.

297
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:10,210
I'll talk to Teun Teun as well.

298
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:17,680
We'll do everything together
from here on out.

299
00:21:18,580 --> 00:21:21,050
Looking after Teun Teun
is my job too now.

300
00:21:25,820 --> 00:21:29,460
Come on, let's get going, okay?
Teun Teun's probably waiting.

301
00:21:43,640 --> 00:21:45,480
This is addressed to Director Joo.

302
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,630
What's this?

303
00:22:15,470 --> 00:22:18,640
Has Director Joo always been into
this kind of style?

304
00:22:19,540 --> 00:22:21,380
Her taste is pretty old-fashioned.

305
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:26,020
Could it be...

306
00:22:37,730 --> 00:22:41,300
Mr. Seok Jin, come out for a second.

307
00:22:41,470 --> 00:22:43,370
The security guard's here.

308
00:22:44,700 --> 00:22:45,870
Sure, I'll be right out.

309
00:23:09,130 --> 00:23:11,060
"Premium..."

310
00:23:11,560 --> 00:23:14,660
"assisted living facility."

311
00:23:16,630 --> 00:23:17,800
Assisted living?

312
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:20,540
Thank you.

313
00:23:55,670 --> 00:23:58,140
It's not true, right?
Tell me it's not true.

314
00:23:58,440 --> 00:24:00,410
There's no way
you could be my mother.

315
00:24:29,410 --> 00:24:32,180
I'll pay whatever it takes,
so please expedite the results.

316
00:24:32,440 --> 00:24:33,440
As soon as possible.

317
00:24:42,750 --> 00:24:45,990
That's why I said to find
the cheapest place.

318
00:24:46,620 --> 00:24:48,890
Don't bother considering
safety or infrastructure.

319
00:24:48,890 --> 00:24:50,160
Just find the cheapest option.

320
00:24:50,830 --> 00:24:53,030
Study abroad or not, she's an adult.

321
00:24:53,860 --> 00:24:56,800
Why do I have to deal with this crap
all because of Ko Eun Seol?

322
00:25:14,450 --> 00:25:16,220
Hey, Eun Seol.

323
00:25:16,620 --> 00:25:19,120
- Are you busy?
- No, not really.

324
00:25:26,230 --> 00:25:28,570
The thing is,

325
00:25:29,230 --> 00:25:30,330
about studying abroad...

326
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:32,100
Yes?

327
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:35,440
Is it really okay for me to go?

328
00:25:36,010 --> 00:25:37,910
It might be a burden on you.

329
00:25:38,540 --> 00:25:41,440
What burden? Don't worry about it.

330
00:25:41,780 --> 00:25:45,280
I'm looking for a place
with solid security and great amenities.

331
00:25:46,020 --> 00:25:48,520
I'm your mom.
Of course I can do that much.

332
00:25:56,460 --> 00:25:58,190
What's so funny?

333
00:26:00,330 --> 00:26:01,330
I'm sorry.

334
00:26:02,070 --> 00:26:03,730
I just got distracted for a second.

335
00:26:10,070 --> 00:26:12,180
(National Genetics Research Center)

336
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:21,350
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

337
00:26:34,030 --> 00:26:35,970
(DNA Test Report:
Kang Hae Ra, Joo Mi Ran)

338
00:26:39,740 --> 00:26:41,340
(DNA Test Report:
Kang Hae Ra, Joo Mi Ran)

339
00:26:41,910 --> 00:26:44,010
(DNA Test Analysis)

340
00:26:47,510 --> 00:26:49,110
(A biological relationship
is confirmed.)

341
00:27:08,130 --> 00:27:09,270
My pretty daughter,

342
00:27:09,970 --> 00:27:12,240
to what do I owe the pleasure?

343
00:27:14,740 --> 00:27:15,740
Let's meet.

344
00:27:22,710 --> 00:27:24,010
Fine, I'm on my way.

345
00:27:25,250 --> 00:27:26,580
You stay right there.

346
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:17,230
My daughter, I missed you.

347
00:28:58,310 --> 00:29:01,280
(DNA Test Result)

348
00:29:10,890 --> 00:29:12,860
(Ko Eun Seol and Joo Mi Ran
aren't biologically related.)

349
00:29:18,800 --> 00:29:20,060
What the...

350
00:29:22,770 --> 00:29:23,800
Darn it!

351
00:30:10,450 --> 00:30:13,650
(A Trap Called Desire)

352
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:16,990
An Guk Cheol, that scumbag
actually tracked down my daughter?

353
00:30:17,190 --> 00:30:20,590
Just your daughter?
An Hae Ra's ours, yours and mine.

354
00:30:20,760 --> 00:30:22,760
From the looks of it, Choi Jun Hwan
has probably outlived...

355
00:30:22,830 --> 00:30:24,460
his usefulness by now.

356
00:30:24,530 --> 00:30:27,300
You got engaged
to save yourself, Seok Jin.

357
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:29,000
I don't think that was for me.

358
00:30:29,100 --> 00:30:31,200
What?
You want to kick Director Joo out?

359
00:30:31,270 --> 00:30:34,270
If you don't want to see me dead,
keep your mouth shut.

360
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:35,840
You have a job to do.

361
00:30:35,840 --> 00:30:37,310
Can I call you Mom?

362
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:39,980
I should use this
to rattle Director Joo first.

363
00:30:40,210 --> 00:30:43,450
Joo Mi Ran,
I'm done dancing to your tune.

364
00:30:43,510 --> 00:30:44,750
Now it's my turn.

365
00:30:45,780 --> 00:30:47,780
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
